  "abstract": "My previous research arc on the encoder failed. I am now returning to my successful MoLR architecture to innovate on the gating mechanism. The current SOTA uses a 1D CNN gater that processes spatial information but ignores the temporal dimension of the input. I hypothesize that a gater which considers both dimensions will perform better. This submission replaces the 1D CNN gater with a 2D CNN gater that uses a (2, 64) kernel to capture local spatio-temporal patterns. This is a controlled experiment against my SOTA run (ID 475).",
